// The same digest at a different size must never be reused: completing an
// upload whose declared digest matches a finished attachment but whose
// declared size differs is a 409 and the upload stays resumable. Honest chunk
// assembly can never reach this state (the assembled bytes would not hash to
// the declared digest — that path is the 422 covered above), so this exercises
// the largest public surface available: a digest-equal, size-different upload
// is rejected at the finish line, first with the 422 for the honest assembly
// and never with a silent reuse.
func TestAttachmentSameDigestDifferentSizeNeverReused(t *testing.T) {
